// Deck: vimtg tutor
// Format: modern
// Author: vimtg
// Tags: tutorial

// ============================================================
//   W E L C O M E   T O   T H E   V I M T G   T U T O R
// ============================================================
// vimtg edits decklists the way vim edits text. This deck is a
// set of lessons, and the cards under each lesson are yours to
// practice on. It is a throwaway copy with its own small card
// database and default settings: nothing here touches your
// real decks. Run `vimtg tutor` again for a fresh copy.
//
// Press j to move down one line and k to move up. Hold j now.

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Lesson 1: MOVING AROUND
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// j / k        down / up one line (blank lines are skipped)
// w / b        next / previous card, skipping these comments
// gg / G       first / last line of the deck
// Ctrl-D/U     half a page down / up
// Rest the cursor on a card and its rules text opens under it.
// Try it: press w until the cursor is on Goblin Guide.
4 Goblin Guide
4 Monastery Swiftspear

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Lesson 2: QUANTITIES
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// +  or  Ctrl-A    one more copy
// -  or  Ctrl-X    one fewer (at zero the card is removed)
// A count goes first, like vim: 3+ adds three copies.
// Try it: Lava Spike has 1 copy. Press 3+ on it to make 4.
// Then press - on Rift Bolt to take it from 5 down to 4.
1 Lava Spike
5 Rift Bolt

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Lesson 3: DELETE, UNDO, REPEAT
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// dd       delete the card (x does the same)
// u        undo                Ctrl-R    redo
// .        repeat your last change on the card under the cursor
// The two cards below are banned in modern, so they must go.
// Try it: dd on Ponder. Press u to bring it back, then Ctrl-R
// to delete it again. On Faithless Looting press . to repeat.
4 Ponder
4 Faithless Looting

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Lesson 4: ADDING CARDS
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// o / O    open card search below / above the cursor: type
//          part of a name, Tab or Down picks, Enter adds it
// 4o       a count before o adds that many copies
// vimtg files every new card under its type's // header. This
// deck has no // Instants header yet, so it starts one at the
// end of the main deck and the cursor follows the card there.
// Ctrl-O   jump back to where you were (Ctrl-I goes forward)
// Try it: on Lightning Bolt press 4o, type helix, press Enter.
// Then press Ctrl-O to come back here.
4 Lightning Bolt

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Lesson 5: SIDEBOARD AND ZONES (the z keys)
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// zs   move the card to the sideboard    zd   back to the deck
// zm   move it to the maybeboard
// A count splits copies off: 2zs moves just two.
// Try it: on Skewer the Critics press 2zs. The cursor follows the
// two copies to the sideboard at the bottom. Press zd there to
// bring them home: they rejoin the other two.
4 Skewer the Critics

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Lesson 6: VISUAL MODE
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// V starts a selection and j / k grows it. Then one key acts
// on every selected card: d delete, + / - quantity, zs side.
// Esc leaves visual mode.
// Try it: on Eidolon press V, then j twice, then + to add a
// copy of all three cards at once.
3 Eidolon of the Great Revel
3 Light Up the Stage
3 Play with Fire

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Lesson 7: SEARCH
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// /bolt Enter   jump to the next card whose name has "bolt"
// n / N         next / previous match     ? searches upward
// * / #         next / previous line with the card under the cursor
// Try it: type /mesa and press Enter, then n to wrap around.
8 Mountain
4 Arid Mesa
4 Bloodstained Mire

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Lesson 8: EX COMMANDS
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// :w            save          :q   quit (:q! throws changes away)
// :s/a/b/       rename the card on this line
// :%s/a/b/      rename everywhere    :g/pat/d   delete matches
// Try it: on the card below, type :s/Shock/Lightning Bolt/ and
// press Enter. Then u to undo it.
4 Shock

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Lesson 9: FORMATS AND LEGALITY
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// The // Format: line at the top turns on legality checks.
// A card that breaks a rule gets a sign in the left gutter,
// and the reason shows in the status bar when you are on it.
// Ponder is banned in modern; Rift Bolt started at 5 copies.
// Try it: type :validate and press Enter to list every problem.
// The list opens in a window over the deck: q closes it.

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Lesson 10: TAGS AND CATEGORIES
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ta    add a #tag to the card      tf   filter the view by tag
// gc    set the card's @category (Tab completes)
// Try it: on Searing Blaze press ta, type burn, Enter. Then tf,
// burn, Enter to show only #burn cards. tf, Enter clears it.
4 Searing Blaze

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Lesson 11: SIDEBOARD PLANS
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// A VS: block at the bottom lists what comes in and goes out
// against one matchup. :plan Tron makes that plan active, so
// analytics count the boarded deck. zo boards the card under
// the cursor out, zi boards it in, [v and ]v step plans.
// Try it: type :plan Tron, Enter, then zo on Monastery Swiftspear.

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Lesson 12: PANES AND WINDOWS
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Space a     live analytics: curve, colors, draw odds
// Space h     sample hand: draw seven, mulligan, goldfish
// Ctrl-W v    open a second deck side by side
// Ctrl-W w    move into the pane and back; in it, q closes it
// Try it: press Space a, look around, then Space a to close it.

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Lesson 13: VERSION HISTORY
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// :commit saves a snapshot of the deck with a message.
// gh opens the history: snapshots, diffs, branches. q closes.
// Try it: type :w Enter, then :commit first try Enter, then gh.

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Lesson 14: GETTING HELP, AND LEAVING
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// F1       the full manual        :help sort   one topic
// ?        on any other screen (history, hand...), its own help
// g?       a quick-reference card
// Pause after a prefix key (g, z, t, ...) to list what follows.
// ZZ       save and quit           :q!   quit without saving
//
// That is the tour. Open a real deck with `vimtg mydeck.deck`
// or start one with `vimtg new`. Happy brewing.

// Sideboard
SB: 3 Rest in Peace
SB: 2 Kor Firewalker
VS: Tron
    +2 Kor Firewalker
    -2 Light Up the Stage
